  I am not an expert on Noh by any means, but even I can see that this actor is a master of his craft.

  Each step, each gallant sweep of his fan, rings with a warrior's power.

  And his voice. His㉒<I>voice.</I> 
  I have heard nothing like it.

  Other actors have impressed me with their rhythm and tone, but none has ever infused his technique with such pathos. The strains of his sorrow grip my heart, as if I were the warrior fated to die.

  Who is this man who weaves such beauty? If I had to guess, I'd place him a disciple of the Kongo school...

